"Let $T$ be a tournament, let $C_{\\ell}$ be the directed cycle of length $\\ell$, and let $t(C_{\\ell},T)$ denote its homomorphism density. For each $\\ell$, let $g_{\\ell}$ be the function defined by the random blow-up construction, and let $\\alpha_{\\ell}$ be the constant appearing in the source's asymptotic bounds for regular tournaments. **$4k+2$ cycle conjecture.** For every integer $\\ell\\geq6$ with $\\ell\\equiv2\\pmod4$, every tournament $T$ satisfies\n\n$$\nt(C_{\\ell},T)\\geq 2^{\\ell}\\alpha_{\\ell}\\,g_{\\ell}(t(C_3,T))+o(1),\n$$\n\nwhere $o(1)\\to0$ as $|V(T)|\\to\\infty$. This proposes the optimal lower bound for the cycle-minimization problem in the congruence class where the random blow-up bound fails; even determining the asymptotic minimum for $C_6$ in regular tournaments is open."